PART 3: LANDAU POLYTOPE — INTEGER POINT COUNT GROWTH
------------------------------------------------------------

  n=2:      1 score sequences, ratio to prev = inf
  n=3:      2 score sequences, ratio to prev = 2.000
  n=4:      4 score sequences, ratio to prev = 2.000
  n=5:      9 score sequences, ratio to prev = 2.250
  n=6:     22 score sequences, ratio to prev = 2.444
  n=7:     59 score sequences, ratio to prev = 2.682
  n=8:    167 score sequences, ratio to prev = 2.831

  Growth is roughly 2.5-2.8x per n step.
  Compare: iso class counts grow ~3× per n step (from S174).
  Score sequences grow SLOWER than iso classes →
  the average FIBER (iso classes per score seq) INCREASES with n.

  FIBER SIZES AT n=5 (iso classes per score sequence):
                   score   # tournaments              H values  # H vals
         (0, 1, 2, 3, 4)             120                   [1]         1
         (0, 1, 3, 3, 3)              40                   [3]         1
         (0, 2, 2, 2, 4)              40                   [3]         1
         (0, 2, 2, 3, 3)             120                   [5]         1
         (1, 1, 1, 3, 4)              40                   [3]         1
         (1, 1, 2, 2, 4)             120                   [5]         1
         (1, 1, 2, 3, 3)             240                   [9]         1
         (1, 2, 2, 2, 3)             280          [11, 13, 15]         3
         (2, 2, 2, 2, 2)              24                  [15]         1

  Most score sequences at n=5 determine H uniquely.
  Only (1,1,2,3,3) and (0,2,2,3,3) have >1 H value → they're AMBIGUOUS.
  These are exactly the score sequences containing iso class SPLITS.


